==Rice Bowl==
{{Main|Rice Bowl}}
The '''Rice Bowl''' ({{nihongo|ライスボウル|Raisu Bōru}}) is the X-League's national championship game and the single most anticipated event in the Sanese Lurandian Football calendar. Held annually on the second Saturday of January, the game determines the X-League champion and has become a de facto national holiday, with viewership routinely exceeding 40 million.

[[File:Rice Bowl trophy.jpg|thumb|The Rice Bowl trophy]]

The Rice Bowl was first held in 1979, six years before the formal establishment of the X-League, as a championship game for the existing corporate amateur circuit. The game was retained as the championship event when the X-League was founded in 1985. The name was chosen to honor the grain that forms the cultural and dietary cornerstone of Sanese civilization.

